\begin{align*}
\frac{2^{n+4} - 2(2^n)}{2(2^{n+3})} &= \frac{2^n \cdot 2^4 - 2 \cdot 2^n}{2 \cdot 2^n \cdot 2^3} \\
&= \frac{16 \cdot 2^n - 2 \cdot 2^n}{2 \cdot 2^n \cdot 8} \\
&= \frac{14 \cdot 2^n}{16 \cdot 2^n} \\
&= \frac{14}{16} \\
&= \boxed{\frac{7}{8}}.
\end{align*}
The answer is: \frac{7}{8}

